tps://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/deployments","created_at":"2018-11-27T03:35:03Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T09:08:20Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-10T20:45:00Z","git_url":"git://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy","homepage":"https://www.sqlalchemy.org","size":99269,"stargazers_count":11252,"watchers_count":11252,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1606,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":205,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["python","sql","sqlalchemy"],"visibility":"public","forks":1606,"open_issues":205,"watchers":11252,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nAfter upgrading to SQLAlchemy 2.0, one of our queries broke because in the new version, using the `.ilike()` column operator doesn't do what it used to do. \r\n\r\nWe are using database reflection to load the models, but this is the basis of the column definitions:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass Address(Base):\r\n    state = Column(ForeignKey(\"states.code\", ondelete=\"SET DEFAULT\", onupdate=\"CASCADE\"), nullable=False)\r\n\r\nclass State(Base):\r\n    code = Column(CHAR(2), primary_key=True)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you notice in the code to reproduce section, casting the string to VARCHAR(2) completely changes the where condition of the query.\n\n### Optional link from https://docs.sqlalchemy.org which documents the behavior that is expected\n\nhttps://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/20/core/metadata.html#sqlalchemy.schema.Column.ilike\n\n### SQLAlchemy Version in Use\n\n2.0.7\n\n### DBAPI (i.e. the database driver)\n\npsycopg (async)\n\n### Database Vendor and Major Version\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.8\n\n### Operating system\n\nLinux and Windows\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nasync def main():\r\n    async with AsyncSession() as session:\r\n        stmt = sa.select(public.Address.street).where(public.Address.state.ilike(\"%sd%\"))\r\n        results = (await session.execute(stmt)).all()\r\n        print(results)\r\n\r\nawait main()\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\n2023-03-24 14:59:31,632 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine BEGIN (implicit)\r\n2023-03-24 14:59:31,664 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine SELECT addresses.street \r\nFROM addresses \r\nWHERE addresses.state ILIKE %(state_1)s::VARCHAR(2)\r\n2023-03-24 14:59:31,671 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [generated in 0.00980s] {'state_1': '%sd%'}\r\n[]\r\n2023-03-24 14:59:31,882 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine ROLLBACK\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9541/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"purplesmoke05","id":15183665,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTgzNjY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15183665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05","html_url":"https://github.com/purplesmoke05","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/purplesmoke05/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-04-07T01:03:02Z","updated_at":"2023-04-07T01:03:02